The goal of Day 1 is to bridge the gap between theoretical cluster architecture and hands-on, production-grade DevOps practices. By the end of this session, you will understand:

How Kubernetes control plane and worker node components interact under the hood.

How to set up and manage a local development cluster using Minikube in GitHub Codespaces.

How to deploy and manage workloads declaratively using Deployments, ReplicaSets, and Pods.

How to decouple application settings using ConfigMaps and Secrets.

How internal service discovery works via Services, Endpoints, and EndpointSlices.

Real-world troubleshooting techniques for container configuration errors.